  "notes": "Miami’s punk-rap loudest-mix lane, defined by producer partnerships rather than by melody. Harmonic movement is **essentially absent — the loop is a timbre, not a progression** — so the model is a static minor pentatonic i with one dark synth or bell loop. The 808 is very forward with a medium decay and one slide per two bars, frequently doubled an octave up to cut through a clipped drum bus. ⚠ **`low`**: chart, label and collaborators are documented, but the research says there is **no sourced statement about his own method**, so the drum grammar is inherited from the lane.",
